{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1553738-scion-of-zephyrus","id":1553738,"title":"Scion of Zephyrus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-09-10T13:37:22-07:00","id":1553738,"title":"Scion of Zephyrus","content":"Zephyrus, god of the West wind, husband of Iris goddess of the rainbow, and the most beloved of the Anemoi. I assume that Zephyrus has several purviews. Although Hermes and Iris are sent when you deliver a message, when you need to deliver things or people, the Olympians sent Zephyrus, so he must have Journeys purview. As God of West wind he must have the Sky purview. Zephyrus is associated with flowers and fertility. Purviews involving human, animal and plant Fertility seem right. Epic Strength and Dexterity seem likely. As harvest time in ancient Greece was in the spring (wheat would die in summer, you planted in fall, it grew through the mild winter, and you harvested in spring) I assume that Zephyrus also has the Prosperity purview, at least in Agriculture. <br /> <br /> Does a Scion of Zephyrus seem reasonable with choices among the Metamorphosis, Journeys, Sky, Fertility, Health, and Prosperity Purviews, and Epic Strength and Dexterity, seem reasonable. <br /> <br /> Reactions,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-10-2025, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-18T03:58:13-07:00","id":1558919,"title":"","content":"I think most of those could work; I'm not sure of the rationale for Epic Strength, though. I would consider giving Zephyrus Artistry (Music), as the West Wind is associated with both the aulos and with singing. What Callings would you consider? I think Liminal and Lover would be appropriate, but I don't know what to do for a third.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28946-pryderi","name":"Pryderi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-18T08:12:43-07:00","id":1558924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pryderi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1553738-scion-of-zephyrus?p=1558919#post1558919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think most of those could work; I'm not sure of the rationale for Epic Strength, though. I would consider giving Zephyrus Artistry (Music), as the West Wind is associated with both the aulos and with singing. What Callings would you consider? I think Liminal and Lover would be appropriate, but I don't know what to do for a third.</div> </div> </div> </div>My justification for <b>Epic Strength </b>is that Zephyrus was the delivery service. Isis was sent with messages and some forms of weather, Hermes was sent when it was important that the message be taken seriously, either in the case of Hermes providing guidance or Hermes being the troubleshooter for Olympus. Zephyrus was sent to deliver things and people. Zephyrus physically took cargo to wherever the Olympians wanted it to go. I assume that requires Strength. Also, gods of the wind are traditionally depicted as strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-18T23:56:59-07:00","id":1558934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1553738-scion-of-zephyrus?p=1558924#post1558924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My justification for <b>Epic Strength </b>is that Zephyrus was the delivery service. Isis was sent with messages and some forms of weather, Hermes was sent when it was important that the message be taken seriously, either in the case of Hermes providing guidance or Hermes being the troubleshooter for Olympus. Zephyrus was sent to deliver things and people. Zephyrus physically took cargo to wherever the Olympians wanted it to go. I assume that requires Strength. Also, gods of the wind are traditionally depicted as strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that actually makes sense. I hadn't thought about it like that. I'd still lean toward including Artistry (Music) or Artistry (Wind Instruments) as well, given his association with the aulos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28946-pryderi","name":"Pryderi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-19T02:26:05-07:00","id":1558935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pryderi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1553738-scion-of-zephyrus?p=1558934#post1558934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, that actually makes sense. I hadn't thought about it like that. I'd still lean toward including Artistry (Music) or Artistry (Wind Instruments) as well, given his association with the aulos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the additional purviews. They make sense. How would you handle the other Anemoi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-25T10:18:13-07:00","id":1559011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1553738-scion-of-zephyrus?p=1558935#post1558935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the additional purviews. They make sense. How would you handle the other Anemoi?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, good question...Other than Boreas, there isn't much to go on. I'd go with the following (there are probably other appropriate Purviews that I'm missing):<br /> Boreas, the north wind: <b>Beasts-Horses </b>(he was closely associated with horses and took the form of a horse to mate with 3,000 mares), <b>Cold</b> (the north wind was associated with freezing temperatures), <b>Epic Strength</b> (he carried off people and once tried to impress a nymph by ripping trees out of the ground; he also competed with Helios to prove who was the stronger god), <b>Sky</b> (self-explanatory).<br /> Notus, the south wind: <b>Sky</b> (self-explanatory) and <b>Water</b> (he's considered the rain-bringer). Maybe also <b>Fire</b> (he's also seen as a dry, desiccating wind, but so is his brother Euros.<br /> Eurus, the east (or southeast) wind: Maybe<b> Fire </b>(he's seen as a dry or hot wind, although I feel this is kind of a stretch), <b>Sky</b> (once again, self-explanatory) and <b>Water </b>(he's also a rain bringer).<br /> Notus and Eurus are difficult, since they hardly have any individual role in mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28946-pryderi","name":"Pryderi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}